  <div class="kg-hero-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="kg-kicker">Kaggriculture · 720-turn economic control · replay-aware execution</div>
      <h1>🌾 Queue-Aware Farming</h1>
      <div class="kg-hero-copy"><p>
        A complete season route does the heavy lifting. Runtime logic stays narrow: repair local WEED disruptions,
        rank shared-market pressure, and preempt a near-clone's predictable premium sale while repaying the shifted quantity exactly.
      </p></div>
      <div class="kg-chip-row">
        <div class="kg-chip">720-turn route</div><div class="kg-chip">Local WEED repair</div>
        <div class="kg-chip">Demand-aware SELL ordering</div><div class="kg-chip">Multi-horizon clone preemption</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kg-stat-row">
        <div class="kg-stat"><span class="v">720</span><span class="k">turns coordinated as one season</span></div>
        <div class="kg-stat"><span class="v">4</span><span class="k">small, purpose-built control layers</span></div>
        <div class="kg-stat"><span class="v">1</span><span class="k">exact <code>main.py</code> validated and archived</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="kg-thesis">
      <div class="label">Controller thesis</div>
      <div class="big">Freeze the strong route. Adapt only where the environment can invalidate or strand value.</div>
      <div class="point"><b>Season route:</b> coordinates capital, labor, crops, livestock, logistics, and planned sales.</div>
      <div class="point"><b>Local repair:</b> a WEED obstruction is treated as a transaction—DIG, retry, then rejoin the route.</div>
      <div class="point"><b>Market timing:</b> existing SELL slots are ranked by price impact and observed town demand.</div>
      <div class="point"><b>Clone preemption:</b> when public farm state is nearly symmetric, move a safe future premium sale earlier—prefer three turns, then two, then one—and subtract exactly the same quantity later.</div>
      <div class="kg-microbar"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
