<div class="kg-prose"><div class="lead">Four findings survived the whole build. They are ordered by how much they changed the design, not by how obvious they look in hindsight.</div></div>

<div class="kg-insight-row">
  <div class="kg-insight"><div class="n">01</div><div class="t">Separation of concerns is the whole design</div><div class="d">A season route owns capital and logistics; runtime owns only what the environment can invalidate. Every attempt to blur that line made the agent less predictable without making it richer.</div></div>
  <div class="kg-insight"><div class="n">02</div><div class="t">Price is a shared, stateful resource</div><div class="d">Both players sell into one inventory. That makes sell <i>ordering</i> a first-class decision and makes any single-agent price model an approximation the moment an opponent exists.</div></div>
  <div class="kg-insight"><div class="n">03</div><div class="t">Timing adaptation must be repaid</div><div class="d">Preemption moves quantity earlier and removes the same quantity when it came due. Without that invariant, a timing layer silently becomes a production change and the route's economics stop holding.</div></div>
</div>

<div class="kg-takeaway">
  <div class="label">Verdict</div>
  <ul>
