<div class="kg-note ember"><div class="title">The key operating insight</div><div class="body">A high spot price can still be a bad decision if the crop takes too long, consumes scarce labor, or crashes after repeated sales. Good play is about <b>economic timing</b>, not just expensive items.</div></div>


<div class="kg-note ice"><div class="title">Current town-demand regime</div><div class="body">The Town Center now removes one of each non-fertilizer product <b>once per day at a flat rate</b>. Shops unlock <b>with replacement</b>, so duplicate shop instances can concentrate demand on a small set of products. The controller therefore reads the live shop list instead of assuming a balanced town.</div></div>
