<div class="kg-note"><div class="title">Small blast radius, by design</div><div class="body">Ordinary turns do not invent purchases or re-plan workers globally. Preemption activates only when the two public farm states are extremely close. A shifted premium quantity is recorded as a debt and removed from the corresponding future SELL, so the overlay changes <b>timing</b>, not intended production volume.</div></div>


<div class="kg-takeaway">
  <div class="label">Takeaway · Section 4</div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Two clocks, two controllers.</b> Season-scale capital and logistics belong to the route; turn-scale correction belongs to runtime. Mixing them is what makes agents brittle.</li>
    <li><b>Small blast radius is a feature.</b> Ordinary turns invent no purchases and re-plan no workers, so a runtime bug can cost a turn but cannot corrupt the season.</li>
    <li><b>Only three things justify overriding the plan:</b> a physical obstruction, the order of orders in a shared queue, and a rival reaching the same premium sale first.</li>
