<div class="kg-terminal">
<span class="dim">live observation</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
read the coordinated season action<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
repair a local WEED obstruction when needed<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
repay any premium quantity shifted from this turn<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
rank existing SELL slots by <b>price impact + live demand urgency</b><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
if public farms are near clones, inspect premium SELLs <b>3 turns ahead</b><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
move a safe quantity now; otherwise fall back to 2 turns, then 1<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
skip preemption at the $1 floor; liquidate terminal leftovers near the deadline<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;↓<br>
return farmer + hands + market orders
</div>

<div class="kg-note"><div class="title">Reusable design principle</div><div class="body">A strong runtime layer should have a <b>small blast radius</b>. The route handles capital and logistics; WEED repair protects physical execution; demand-aware ranking protects the shared queue; clone preemption changes only the timing of bounded premium quantity and carries an explicit repayment debt. Outside the tight clone gate, the route remains unchanged.</div></div>","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00978,"end_time":"2026-08-08T16:25:17.273684+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-08-08T16:25:17.263904+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]}},{"id":"527a7923","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 11. Build, inspect, and rerun the submission archive

